  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 246 AM MST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nOn Monday, upper-level ensemble guidance is in agreement for \nbrief zonal flow over the area before turning into southwesterly\nflow as a trough over the Four Corners region starts moving \neastward. On Tuesday and Wednesday, the trough is expected to \npass by just south of the area and amplify into the southeast \nwhile a deep ridge forms over the Rockies putting us into \nnorthwesterly flow later on Wednesday. Although, as the trough \nis expected to amplify, GEFS mean spread starts to show a little\nbit of uncertainty with the system on Tuesday morning. this \ncould indicate amplification even further to the south and \nsteepen the northwesterly flow on Wednesday. On Thursday, it \nbecomes unclear with the evolution of the overall pattern as the\nridge moves to the south. However with the uncertainty, there \nis medium confidence (40%) that the trough would not amplify \nfurther south. \n\nWith the overall pattern being primarily northwesterly,\ntemperatures for next week are forecast to remain within\nseasonal averages. Afternoon highs are expected to slightly\ndecrease into the upper 30s on Tuesday as the trough moves \nthrough and slowly warm back up with temperatures being in the \n40s for the remainder of the week. Morning Lows are expected to \nfollow a similar trend with the afternoon temperatures, but \nwould likely stay in the 20s.\n\nOn Monday night and Tuesday morning, there could be a chance for\nsnowfall to occur as moist air being fed into the area on Monday\nand a cold front associated with the trough early Tuesday\nmorning. Ensemble is now favoring snowfall to be the predominate\nprecipitation type with this event with GEFS and LREF 6hr 0.1\ninch probabilities now show a 20-30% chance for snow to\naccumulate over the Tri-State area. Though, once temperatures\nstart to rise back to above freezing, we can expect this system\nto dissipate in the afternoon. With this being said, confidence\nfor snow fall has increase slightly to low to medium (25-40%) \nto occur as guidance is favoring the overall pattern to not \namplify to the south.",
